<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39069" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pro-spĕcŭlor</span></b> ,
			āri, v. n. and <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Neutr.</i>, <i>to look into the
				distance</i>, <i>look out</i> (very rare): de
			vallo, Auct. B. Afr. 31.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>to explore</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">L. Siccium prospeculatum ad locum castris
					capiendum mittunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					3, 43, 2</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>to look out for</i>, <i>watch for</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prospeculari e muris adventum imperatoris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					33, 1, 3</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>